            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: What permits are required for commercial paving or site development in Lexington, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates reviews all project plans with the Lexington Department of Public Works and Engineering Division prior to site work. Standard driveway maintenance does not require permits, but commercial parking lot repaving, storm drain connections, or major site excavation requires approval from the Lexington Planning Board and Building Department. S. Phaneuf & Associates manages all municipal permitting filings, traffic control detail logistics, and environmental siltation compliance.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How does S. Phaneuf & Associates repair failing commercial parking lots in Lexington, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates evaluates structural sub-base conditions using heavy test-rolling. Damaged pavement sections are removed using commercial asphalt milling machines. Crews repair underlying sub-base soils with compacted crushed gravel, apply a tack coat adhesive, and lay a dense 2-inch hot-mix asphalt overlay. Final steps include extruding Cape Cod berms, sealing joints, and applying high-visibility traffic line striping compliant with Lexington commercial codes.</p>
